{"id": "bb0b827f-176f-4fe4-8245-1232cc37d82e", "slug": "auraglow-adaptive-dermal-intelligence", "title": "AuraGlow - Adaptive Dermal Intelligence", "description": "Auraglow Adaptive Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. It is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"AuraGlow - Adaptive Dermal Intelligence\"\ndescription: \"Auraglow Adaptive Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. It is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#10B981\"\n  secondary: \"#F59E0B\"\n  accent: \"#F59E0B\"\n  background: \"#0F1115\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Playfair Display\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# AuraGlow - Adaptive Dermal Intelligence\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 34; favorites: 5; remixes: 0.\nTags: hero, section, animated, webgl, threejs, cta, effect.\n## Overview\nAuraglow Adaptive Hero Section is designed for introducing a product with clear above-the-fold messaging. Key features include headline hierarchy, supporting copy, and a primary call-to-action. It is suitable for homepage hero areas and campaign landing pages.\n\nAuraGlow Eliminate skincare uncertainty. Stop relying on trial and error. Embrace an adaptive neural-engine that illuminates your authentic radiance. Adaptive dermal intelligence AURAGLOW © 2026 18'\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Adaptive dermal intelligence; AURAGLOW.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #10B981, secondary #F59E0B, accent #F59E0B, background #0F1115, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Playfair Display for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nAuthentication and CTA controls should preserve the source button hierarchy, input density, and focused conversion path.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>AuraGlow - Adaptive Dermal Intelligence</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Playfair+Display:ital@0;1&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-black text-white m-0 p-0 overflow-x-hidden antialiased min-h-[150vh] relative selection:bg-emerald-500/30\" style=\"font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\">\n\n    <!-- WebGL Background Container -->\n    <div id=\"webgl-container\" class=\"fixed top-0 left-0 w-full h-full -z-10 pointer-events-none\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Main UI Overlay -->\n    <div class=\"fixed top-0 left-0 w-full h-screen flex flex-col justify-between pointer-events-none\">\n        \n        <!-- Header -->\n        <header class=\"w-full flex justify-between items-center p-6 md:p-10 pointer-events-auto z-50\">\n            <div class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl tracking-tight\" style=\"font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;\">AuraGlow</div>\n            \n            <!-- Custom Hamburger Toggle -->\n            <button class=\"flex flex-col gap-1.5 w-8 items-end hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity duration-300\" aria-label=\"Menu\">\n                <span class=\"block w-full h-0.5 bg-white rounded-full\"></span>\n                <span class=\"block w-2/3 h-0.5 bg-white rounded-full\"></span>\n            </button>\n        </header>\n\n        <!-- Main Content Area -->\n        <main class=\"flex-1 relative w-full h-full p-6 md:p-10 flex flex-col justify-end\">\n            \n            <!-- Mid-Left Text Block -->\n            <div class=\"absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 left-6 md:left-16 lg:left-24 max-w-sm pointer-events-auto\">\n                <p class=\"js-reveal text-sm md:text-base font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-100\">\n                    Eliminate skincare uncertainty. Stop relying on trial and error. Embrace an adaptive neural-engine that illuminates your authentic radiance.\n                </p>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Bottom Left Title Section -->\n            <div class=\"mb-4 md:mb-12 md:ml-14 pointer-events-auto relative z-10\">\n                <h2 class=\"text-lg md:text-2xl tracking-tight font-normal mb-2 md:mb-4 text-gray-200\">Adaptive dermal intelligence</h2>\n                \n                <!-- Gradient Masked Title -->\n                <h1 id=\"main-title\" class=\"text-6xl md:text-8xl lg:text-9xl font-semibold tracking-tighter uppercase leading-none\" \n                    style=\"background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #10b981 0%, #059669 25%, #fbbf24 50%, #f59e0b 75%, #10b981 100%); background-size: 200% auto; -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; color: transparent;\">\n                    AURAGLOW\n                </h1>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Right Side Vertical Indicators -->\n            <div class=\"absolute right-6 md:right-10 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center gap-6 pointer-events-auto text-xs tracking-widest text-gray-300 mix-blend-difference\" \n                 style=\"writing-mode: vertical-rl; transform: rotate(180deg);\">\n                <span class=\"opacity-80\">© 2026</span>\n                \n                <div class=\"flex gap-2 h-16 items-center justify-center opacity-60\">\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-1.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-1.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-2.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-1.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-4 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-1.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                    <span class=\"w-px h-1.5 bg-white block\"></span>\n                </div>\n                \n                <span class=\"opacity-80\">18'</span>\n            </div>\n            \n        </main>\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // --- WebGL Background Animation (Three.js) ---\n        const initWebGL = () => {\n            const container = document.getElementById('webgl-container');\n            const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n            \n            const camera = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n            \n            const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, alpha: true });\n            renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n            renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n            container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n            const geometry = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(2, 2);\n\n            const vertexShader = `\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n                void main() {\n                    vUv = uv;\n                    gl_Position = vec4(position, 1.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            // Procedural fluid-like shader with Emerald / Gold palette\n            const fragmentShader = `\n                uniform float u_time;\n                uniform vec2 u_resolution;\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n\n                // Color palette based on requested change\n                vec3 colorA = vec3(0.04, 0.59, 0.41); // Emerald Green\n                vec3 colorB = vec3(0.98, 0.75, 0.14); // Gold/Amber\n                vec3 colorC = vec3(0.06, 0.73, 0.51); // Teal\n                vec3 colorD = vec3(0.02, 0.15, 0.08); // Dark Emerald Base\n\n                void main() {\n                    vec2 st = gl_FragCoord.xy / u_resolution.xy;\n                    st.x *= u_resolution.x / u_resolution.y;\n                    \n                    vec2 q = vec2(0.);\n                    q.x = st.x + u_time * 0.1;\n                    q.y = st.y - u_time * 0.05;\n                    \n                    float noise1 = sin(q.x * 5.0 + sin(u_time * 0.5)) * cos(q.y * 3.0 + u_time * 0.2);\n                    float noise2 = sin(q.y * 4.0 - u_time * 0.3) * cos(q.x * 6.0 - sin(u_time * 0.4));\n                    \n                    float finalNoise = (noise1 + noise2) * 0.5;\n                    \n                    vec3 color = mix(colorD, colorA, smoothstep(-1.0, 0.5, finalNoise));\n                    color = mix(color, colorB, smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, finalNoise * sin(u_time * 0.5 + st.x * 10.0)));\n                    color = mix(color, colorC, smoothstep(0.5, 1.0, finalNoise * cos(u_time * 0.3 + st.y * 5.0)));\n                    \n                    // Add subtle vignette/darkening to edges\n                    float vignette = distance(vUv, vec2(0.5));\n                    color *= smoothstep(0.9, 0.2, vignette);\n\n                    gl_FragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n                vertexShader,\n                fragmentShader,\n                uniforms: {\n                    u_time: { value: 0.0 },\n                    u_resolution: { value: new THREE.Vector2(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight) }\n                }\n            });\n\n            const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n            scene.add(mesh);\n\n            const clock = new THREE.Clock();\n\n            const animate = () => {\n                requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n                material.uniforms.u_time.value = clock.getElapsedTime();\n                renderer.render(scene, camera);\n            };\n\n            animate();\n\n            window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n                renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n                material.uniforms.u_resolution.value.set(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n            });\n        };\n\n        // --- GSAP Animations & Interactions ---\n        const initAnimations = () => {\n            gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n            // Masked Staggered Word Reveal\n            const revealTextEl = document.querySelector('.js-reveal');\n            if (revealTextEl) {\n                const words = revealTextEl.innerText.split(' ');\n                revealTextEl.innerHTML = '';\n                \n                words.forEach(word => {\n                    const outerSpan = document.createElement('span');\n                    outerSpan.style.cssText = 'overflow: hidden; display: inline-flex; vertical-align: top; margin-right: 0.25em; padding-bottom: 0.1em;';\n                    \n                    const innerSpan = document.createElement('span');\n                    innerSpan.className = 'reveal-word';\n                    innerSpan.textContent = word;\n                    innerSpan.style.cssText = 'display: inline-block; transform: translateY(110%);';\n                    \n                    outerSpan.appendChild(innerSpan);\n                    revealTextEl.appendChild(outerSpan);\n                });\n\n                gsap.to('.reveal-word', {\n                    y: '0%',\n                    duration: 1.2,\n                    stagger: 0.04,\n                    ease: 'power4.out',\n                    scrollTrigger: {\n                        trigger: 'body', // Trigger on body scroll\n                        start: 'top top',\n                        end: 'bottom bottom',\n                        scrub: 1, // Tie to scroll progress for dynamic reveal\n                        toggleActions: 'play none none reverse'\n                    }\n                });\n\n                // Fallback animation on load if user doesn't scroll immediately\n                gsap.to('.reveal-word', {\n                    y: '0%',\n                    duration: 1.2,\n                    stagger: 0.04,\n                    ease: 'power4.out',\n                    delay: 0.5\n                });\n            }\n\n            // Animate Gradient Text Background\n            gsap.to('#main-title', {\n                backgroundPositionX: '200%',\n                duration: 10,\n                ease: 'none',\n                repeat: -1\n            });\n        };\n\n        // Initialize on load\n        window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n            initWebGL();\n            initAnimations();\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "auraglow-adaptive-dermal-intelligence.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/auraglow-adaptive-dermal-intelligence.jpg", "source_name": "auraglow-adaptive-dermal-intelligence-DESIGN.md", "views": 77, "forks": 2, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-06-12T07:38:10.793894+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T09:24:46.417116+00:00"}